// The standard content library (P3B.5, `intro-to-assemblies.md` A19, X12): fasteners generated
// as parametric parts by `cadrs_core::assembly::standard`. Every size row records where its
// dimensions come from. Dimensions are in the standard's own unit (inch for ANSI, mm for ISO):
//
// - `d`: nominal (major) diameter; the shank, and the nut's or washer's bore.
// - `f`: width across flats (basic for ANSI; s max for ISO). `g`: width across corners, as the
//   table gives it (G max / e min); the generator draws the exact hexagon of `f`, whose corners
//   are f·2/√3.
// - `h`: head height, nut thickness or washer thickness (basic for ANSI; k or m max for ISO).
// - `head`: head diameter (pan head A max, socket head dk max) or washer outside diameter.
// - `inner`: washer inside diameter. `socket`: hexagon socket size s. `slot`: slot width J max.
//
// Threads are drawn as plain cylinders of the nominal diameter (the thread form is not modelled).
// Lengths are the component's catalogue lengths (inch or mm).
Library(
    standards: [
        Standard(
            name: "ANSI inch",
            unit: Inch,
            categories: [
                Category(
                    name: "Bolts & screws",
                    classes: [
                        Class(
